Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.760
Hello.

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:04.720
Hello. We are KANA-BOON. Hi.

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:06.160
Thanks for having us.

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:07.020
Thank you.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:21.540
I'm Maguro Taniguchi, lead vocals and
 guitarist for KANA-BOON. Hello. And then...

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:22.580
I'm Takahiro Koizumi.

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:23.660
Right.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:25.230
I'm the guitarist, Hayato Koga.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:27.050
I'm the bassist, Mashi.

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:28.600
Good morning, good afternoon, 
and good evening. How's everyone doing?

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:30.410
Good morning. Hello.
Good morning, good afternoon, 
and good evening. How's everyone doing?

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:31.930
Good morning, good afternoon, 
and good evening. How's everyone doing?

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:34.060
We have some questions here.

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:35.510
Okay.
We have some questions here.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:38.800
"How did your group form?"

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:40.120
I see. Our formation story.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:45.070
When we were 16-year-old 
first-years in high school,

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:50.400
we met through our 
school's light music club.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:56.190
I said I wanted to form a band, 
and Koi-chan sat next to me.

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:57.880
We sat next to each other.

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:00.020
That's how we met.

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:04.160
And I didn't bring any pencils 
on my first day of high school.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:05.380
You sure didn't.

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:08.760
So I asked Koi-chan to lend me a pen.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:11.670
Then, we joined the 
light music club together.

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:13.900
And these two...

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:15.300
We're childhood friends.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:16.820
Since grade school.

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:20.920
Koi-chan told me he'd been
 invited to join a band...

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:23.240
or rather, invited to 
join the light music club,

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:27.760
so I thought, "Maybe I'll join the club, too."
 It was like a domino effect.

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:32.560
The first band the three of us 
formed together was KANA-BOON.

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:33.260
Yeah.

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:37.420
And we met Mashi in second year.

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:42.880
I was a second-year at another 
high school, but we became friends.

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:49.670
For a long time after that, I was either 
living with Maguro or hanging out as friends.

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:52.550
You joined the band last year.

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:55.210
Last April.

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:57.930
In April 2022, you became a member.

00:01:57.930 --> 00:01:58.970
Yes.

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:02.850
And now, the four of us work together.

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:03.860
Yeah.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:05.420
Next one's about Naruto.

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:06.890
Naruto? Okay.

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:12.500
A lot of foreign fans learned 
of KANA-BOON through Naruto.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:19.610
The people watching this 
probably like Naruto, too.

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:20.300
Yeah.

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:22.490
It's one of Japan's biggest anime series.

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:27.750
"Could you tell us your highlights 
of providing music for Naruto?"

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:29.400
So, like memories, I guess.

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:37.620
Naruto's "Silhouette" was the 
first song we wrote for an anime.

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:39.680
We were so happy.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:41.830
So happy.

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:43.990
Sorry, Mashi. You weren't in the band then.

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:44.640
Right.
Sorry, Mashi. You weren't in the band then.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:45.590
Right.

00:02:45.590 --> 00:02:47.300
So this is just for the three of us.

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:53.960
The Naruto manga started 
while we were still in grade school.

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:56.260
We got really excited 
following the series in real time.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:57.720
Really excited, yeah.
We got really excited 
following the series in real time.

00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:58.520
We got really excited 
following the series in real time.

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:03.990
So working on Naruto had been 
a dream of ours since we debuted.

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:18.590
When that came true and we went to 
the SONY Music office together, I cried.

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:23.420
It's not often that you get to 
experience something that moving,

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:25.680
so I was very happy about it.

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:30.910
Mashi, you watched KANA-BOON do all that.

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:41.940
Your popularity exploded, and you started 
appearing all over the place, including on TV.

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:48.100
I was watching all of that while 
working my regular part-time job.

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:51.430
People get really excited 
for this song at shows,

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:57.750
which always reminds me 
how great and significant it is for us.

00:03:57.750 --> 00:04:03.930
People get really excited for "Silhouette." 
They even sing it in Japanese.

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:10.300
This was true when we released 
the song and it's still true today,

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:14.440
but it always moves us in fresh ways.

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:15.320
Okay.

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:21.200
Oh, I like this question.

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:24.820
It's about the Naruto game.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:31.300
"NARUTO SHIPPUDEN: Ultimate Ninja 
STORM 4's 'Spiral' is awesome," it says.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:32.460
Thank you.

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:36.300
"'Silhouette' is also awesome."

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:46.740
"Could you explain the process 
of writing songs and music for Naruto?"

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:53.400
Our connection with
Naruto is kind of special.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:05:02.190
We followed the manga 
and anime in real time.

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:07.340
We never really felt any pressure.

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:11.570
We're able to naturally produce songs

00:05:11.570 --> 00:05:18.830
just by thinking about what 
Naruto and Boruto mean to us.

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:27.590
We think a little more about the original work
 when we create songs for other series.

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:31.070
We've written about five songs for Naruto,

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:34.730
and we've been able to do it 
in a natural and relaxed way.

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:40.320
We have a kind of mysterious
 affinity with the series.

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:42.740
You know, like Rasengan.

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:50.670
Right. For the Naruto series, I pay extra 
attention to the scenery and technique names,

00:05:50.670 --> 00:05:54.140
and draw inspiration from them.

00:05:54.490 --> 00:06:00.580
I've written phrases trying to 
capture the sound of Rasengan.

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:03.010
He's the one guy in the band 
who can produce a Rasengan.

00:06:03.010 --> 00:06:04.440
I can?

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:06.150
Yeah. Yeah, you can.

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:09.130
Okay.

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:13.160
"We've heard you're big fans of Naruto."

00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:14.680
Yes, of course.

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:21.440
"How does it feel to 
perform Naruto songs live?"

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:28.970
Is there anything we think or feel as fans?

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:37.150
I mentioned it just now, 
but when I write songs or phrases,

00:06:37.150 --> 00:06:41.760
I think about the techniques 
and scenery that appear in Naruto.

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:44.160
I think about those things while playing, too.

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:52.330
I imagine the opening animation 
in my head while I'm playing.

00:06:52.330 --> 00:06:58.220
But when I saw how excited fans were 
in Canada, Indonesia, and Saudi Arabia,

00:06:58.220 --> 00:07:00.570
I couldn't even think about that anymore.

00:07:00.570 --> 00:07:03.730
I wanted to connect with 
the people right in front of me.

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:06.350
When we performed overseas,

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:16.650
I found myself most often thinking 
about the original author, Mr. Kishimoto.

00:07:16.650 --> 00:07:25.440
We've met and spoken to 
Naruto's original author, Mr. Kishimoto.

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:32.430
When we wrote the song "Diver" 
and performed it at an event,

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:37.850
Mr. Kishimoto cried tears of joy.

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:43.260
I remember that specific moment.

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:51.410
So when we perform "Silhouette" overseas, 
I think about Mr. Kishimoto.

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:52.730
Wow.

00:07:52.730 --> 00:07:58.090
Like, "Thank you for bringing us here," and,
 "I wish I could show this to Mr. Kishimoto."

00:07:58.930 --> 00:08:02.020
Yeah. That's what I think about.

00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:06.080
"Aside from Naruto, you've written 
songs for a variety of anime series,

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:09.660
including My Hero Academia, Fire Force,
 and more recently, Zom 100."

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:10.780
Yeah, Zom 100. including My Hero Academia, Fire Force,
 and more recently, Zom 100."

00:08:10.780 --> 00:08:14.130
including My Hero Academia, Fire Force,
 and more recently, Zom 100."

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:22.780
"When you first started out, did you imagine 
you'd end up working on so many amazing series?"

00:08:22.780 --> 00:08:25.340
"Did you expect this to happen?"

00:08:25.340 --> 00:08:27.000
No, no, no.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:27.600
No?

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:30.120
No, definitely not.

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:31.920
No, we didn't.

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:39.700
We always wanted to be a good cool band,

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:48.180
but we never expected to 
work on so many anime series.

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:51.170
Even when we wrote "Silhouette" for Naruto,

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:55.560
we didn't expect to write 
so many more songs for anime series.

00:08:55.560 --> 00:09:00.770
We wanted to work on Naruto, 
so that was something we could imagine,

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:06.030
but working on all these other series
 isn't something we imagined.

00:09:06.030 --> 00:09:07.970
Yeah. It's strange, isn't it?

00:09:07.970 --> 00:09:08.790
It is.

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:11.210
KANA-BOON and anime.

00:09:12.590 --> 00:09:14.200
I guess we're very compatible.

00:09:15.890 --> 00:09:16.760
Okay.

00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:24.360
"The video for My Hero Academia's 
'Starmarker' featuring the disco ball man..."

